  @name "ACT2: Black Brothers"
  @first "Harrenhal Torchlit Census at the rookery"
  @sections "Harrenhal Torchlit Census at the rookery" "Dragonstone Blood Price at first light" "Blackwater Bay Sealed Bargain beneath lion seals" "The Dreadfort Border Muster in crowded galleries" "The Eyrie Crown Ultimatum by candle smoke" "Pentos Harbor Ambush in river fog" "Qarth Alliance Split near the godswood" "The Wall War Map against old law" "Castle Black Inheritance Claim under moonless sky" "Moat Cailin Whispered Warning at the gatehouse" "Oldtown Silent Betrayal behind closed doors" "Pyke Hostage Exchange at the broken tower" "Highgarden Siege Promise in the throne shadow" "Sunspear Prison Confession with steel drawn" "The Trident Salt Pact by the harbor chain" "Riverrun Broken Oath under rain" "The Kingsroad Blackmail Ledger after the feast" "The Red Keep Raven Intercept before the sept bell" "Winterfell Night Council before witnesses" "The Twins Debt Collection under wolf banners" "Harrenhal Torchlit Census at the rookery" "Dragonstone Blood Price at first light" "Blackwater Bay Sealed Bargain beneath lion seals" "The Dreadfort Border Muster in crowded galleries"
__scene

section__
  @title "Harrenhal Torchlit Census at the rookery"
  @textPacing "cinematic"
  @shot "medium"
  @backdrop "https://example.com/thrones/02-act2-arc-nightwatch/frame-145.jpg"

  "In a draft-ridden keep room, lamp oil stings your nose and frost blooms along cracked map tables. Jon Snow presses you to act on relief census rolls that decide who is fed, while Dolorous Edd watches for hesitation that rivals can exploit before the next rider leaves camp. You are not adjudicating theory; you are deciding who moves, who waits, and who pays for that delay.

At the edge of the realm, logistics is survival doctrine. If you force this through public process, you gain legitimacy and lose precious hours. If you handle it through covert pressure, you may buy immediate control while corroding the very cohesion that keeps undermanned outposts alive through winter.

The frontier is under-resourced, and each decision reallocates risk between villages and the Wall. The next order goes out under your name, and it will be judged not by speeches but by how many fires are still lit when night closes again."

  choice__
    @target "Dragonstone Blood Price at first light"
    @action honor = clampStat(honor + 1, 0, 30)
    @action watch_trust = clampStat(watch_trust + 1, 0, 30)
    @action war_readiness = clampStat(war_readiness + 1, 0, 30)
    @action survival_clock = clampStat(survival_clock - 1, 0, 30)
    "Put relief census rolls that decide who is fed before sworn witnesses, bind terms in writing, and accept immediate strain to preserve public legitimacy."
  __choice

  choice__
    @target "Blackwater Bay Sealed Bargain beneath lion seals"
    @action ruthlessness = clampStat(ruthlessness + 1, 0, 30)
    @action secrecy = clampStat(secrecy + 2, 0, 30)
    @action leverage = clampStat(leverage + 1, 0, 30)
    @action survival_clock = clampStat(survival_clock - 1, 0, 30)
    "Handle relief census rolls that decide who is fed through covert channels and selective disclosure, trading transparency for immediate command leverage."
  __choice

  choice__
    @target "The Dreadfort Border Muster in crowded galleries"
    @when ((wealth + essos_ties + dragon_factor) >= 7)
    @action wealth = clampStat(wealth - 1, 0, 30)
    @action war_readiness = clampStat(war_readiness + 1, 0, 30)
    @action essos_ties = clampStat(essos_ties + 1, 0, 30)
    @action dragon_factor = clampStat(dragon_factor + 1, 0, 30)
    @action survival_clock = clampStat(survival_clock - 1, 0, 30)
    "Commit scarce coin and external operators to move relief census rolls that decide who is fed fast, gaining time now while increasing frontier dependency."
  __choice
__section

